Add a new Toy data to the  public.toys   using the data in the consolidated metadata file.
Here is the interface for the Toy table.

interface Toy {
  id: string;
  name?: string;   // from metadata name field 
  title: string;   // from  metadata title field 
  description: string;   // from metadata description field
  price: number;   //  set  
  discountPercentage?: number;
  categoryCode?: number; // from the public table Categories where consoldated category is same as category in Categories 
  inStock: boolean;
  quantity: number;
  imageUrl: string;  // https://<GatewayURL>/ipfs/<QmImageCid> 
  barcodeId?: string; //  is the <QmJsonCid>
  metadata: string; // the consolidated metadata json file url for example  https://<GatewayURL>/ipfs/<QmJsonCid>
}

Refactor the AddToy dashboard as approriate. 
All the text fields  in the AddToy dashboard should be populated with the data from the consolidated metadata file.
Barcode field should be populated with the <QmJsonCid>. It must be readonly and not editable.
The image field should be populated with the imageUrl. It should be readonly and not editable.
The category field should be populated with the category from the consolidated metadata file. It should be readonly and not editable.
Name, Title, Description should be populated with the data from the consolidated metadata file. It should be readonly and not editable.
Price, quantity, in_stock, discountPercentage  should come from the public.toys table and should be editable.
Display  a new discount_price if discountPercentage is not 0. (Price * discountPercentage) / 100.
Display but bar the price field and display the discount_price if discountPercentage is not 0.
